Z||000003||artherd||08-16-2001||04:09 AM||||Lexus' own 32-valve aluminum V8 would make quite a bit more sense, but hey, since the swap is probally going to be total fabrication job, then gm/ford/kia/whoever.  It's a global world incase everyone hasn't noticed :)<P>The Northstar is almost as much classically 'american' as the Dodge Stealth.  It's 4-cam, it's aluminum, and it's reliable. Hardly a typical american design :) (I think this is a good thing...)<P> <BR>I'd be a little scared about the short wheelbase of MR2s, they're a little tiny for me to feel comfortable with a v8.  (and they're going to gain some megga weight too, their stock motor isn't a crappy ass iron boat-anchor good-for-nothing junk heap... sorry, just found my 60k 2.8 has a rod knock :( )  Then again, the fiero could use a wheelbase increase too.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
