Z||000011||artherd||08-21-2001||04:35 AM||||The Lexus V8 is a great engine.<P>I've seen it in several 'retro' hot rods, very very cool.<P>The latest MR2 (the Spyder) is actually a pretty strong car, at least it feels that way :)  Though I dare say 1,000bhp would crumple any production car today. (*under $90,000 let's say. I'm sure the chassis of eg Diablo and F50&lt;no longer made&gt; could and for some lucky bastards, do handle in excess of 1,000bhp :)<P>of course, you don't need *that* :)<BR>The stock engine in an mr2 would be quite the machine, I'd be glad to have one!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>I was thinking of the Lexus V8 for my Fiero. They are plentiful and cheap here being so close to Japan and all. Talked to a guy yesterday (might be buying a Fiero off him actually) who is a hot rodder. Has a mate with a Lexus V8 running 1000 HP. Mega dollar engine but look at that horsepower. Wonder what that would do to a Fiero.  Probably flip it I imagine. <P>Are MR2s strong enough for a Northstar? They certainly aren't as beefed up chassis wise as a Fiero.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
